MEASURED at the delivered parent tree on 2026-09-11. The parent row task-29f36753 is DONE and its gate was daemon 612 files / 11056 passed, exit 0, so the hoist is IN: node-lander.ts now calls checkLandingVerification at ~:212, ABOVE the zero-delivered return at ~:217. Re-measure those line numbers at your own claim HEAD.

1. THE PATTERN TO MIRROR IS TWENTY LINES ABOVE THE DEFECT, in the same function. landOne's observe path reads:
     if (!observed.ok) {
       if (observed.code === 'NOT_A_REPOSITORY') return refuse(...);
       // A git failure that is not structural is reported, not recorded: the next pass retries.
       return { detail: observed.detail, nodeRef, outcome: observed.code };
     }
   One structural code is recorded durably; everything else returns a bare report and the next pass retries. The verification path added directly below it does the opposite for every code:
     if (!checked.ok) return refuse(nodeRef, brief.workspace, verifierReceiptId, { code: checked.code, detail: checked.detail });
   That single line is the defect. The house rule is already written in this file; the second path simply does not follow it.

2. THE CODE THE ROW NAMES IS REAL BUT MISPLACED. VERIFIED_WORKSPACE_GIT_FAILED is not in git-verified-workspace-capture.ts. It is raised in git-verified-workspace-runtime.ts:34 when a git invocation exits non-zero, and in git-verified-workspace-commit.ts:39 and :64. Capture reaches it transitively through the shared verifiedGit invoker. Corrected on the row in comment-6a2a721eb01a4e0c85a8b2b5df37e44a.

3. THE CAPTURE PATH'S OWN CODES, read from git-verified-workspace-capture.ts: VERIFIED_WORKSPACE_DRIFT at :63 when head.headSha or head.branchRef differs from finalHead after the read, plus VERIFIED_WORKSPACE_UNKNOWN, VERIFIED_WORKSPACE_SUBMODULE_UNSUPPORTED, VERIFIED_WORKSPACE_FILTER_UNSUPPORTED and VERIFIED_WORKSPACE_REF_BACKEND_UNSUPPORTED.

4. THE TREE CARRIES TWENTY VERIFIED_WORKSPACE_* CODES, but the roster in scope is only what checkLandingVerification can RETURN: its own three LANDING_ codes plus whatever port.capture() hands back. Enumerate the reachable set from the seam. Classifying unreachable codes is noise; missing a reachable one is the bug repeating.

5. checkLandingVerification's own three: LANDING_VERIFIER_BINDING_MISSING (no matching tested workspace binding), LANDING_VERIFIED_WORKSPACE_UNCONFIGURED (no port), LANDING_VERIFIED_WORKSPACE_CHANGED (sameVerifiedWorkspace false). All three are structural and MUST stay durable - CHANGED especially, since it is the parent row's entire delivery.
